      "thought": "Let $A$ be the number of adult tickets sold and $C$ be the number of child tickets sold.\nThe total number of tickets sold is 120.\n$A + C = 120$ (Equation 1)\n\nThe cost of an adult ticket is 15 euros.\nThe cost of a child ticket is 9 euros.\nThe total revenue is 1476 euros.\n$15A + 9C = 1476$ (Equation 2)\n\nWe need to find the value of $A$.\n\nFrom Equation 1, we can express $C$ in terms of $A$:\n$C = 120 - A$\n\nSubstitute this expression for $C$ into Equation 2:\n$15A + 9(120 - A) = 1476$\n\nNow, solve for $A$:\n$15A + 9 \\times 120 - 9A = 1476$\n$15A + 1080 - 9A = 1476$\n\nCombine the terms involving $A$:\n$(15A - 9A) + 1080 = 1476$\n$6A + 1080 = 1476$\n\nSubtract 1080 from both sides:\n$6A = 1476 - 1080$\n$6A = 396$\n\nDivide by 6:\n$A = 396 / 6$\n$A = 66$\n\nCheck the result:\nIf $A = 66$, then $C = 120 - 66 = 54$.\nTotal revenue = $15A + 9C$\nTotal revenue = $15(66) + 9(54)$\n$15 \\times 66 = 15 \\times (60 + 6) = 900 + 90 = 990$\n$9 \\times 54 = 9 \\times (50 + 4) = 450 + 36 = 486$\nTotal revenue = $990 + 486 = 1476$\nThe total revenue matches the given information.\n\nThe number of adult tickets sold is 66.",
